WEBVTT

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:01.890
Machi!

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:03.650
Machi!

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.980
Let's do this next.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:09.730
What?

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.990
Maybe later.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:18.240
Hey, what's with that unenthusiastic attitude?

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:21.250
Where's all your motivation from last time?

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.330
It's like my battery's run dry.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:29.250
I promise I'll work on it later.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.800
But for now, I need to recharge.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.770
You only went to Uniqlo.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:44.730
And in Yoshio's car, even.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:46.770
You don't understand, Natsu!

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.520
I was frantically struggling with paying

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.860
while enduring those two's
jokes and sexual harassment!

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:56.280
It sounds like quite the ordeal.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:00.580
I understand your pain, but you still need to get up.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.080
Fuchi will yell at you.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.130
Come on, Machi!

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.930
Shall we perform kagura today?

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:18.640
What?

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:21.560
Shall we?

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.820
Kagura is song and dance

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.410
performed as worship, often in shrines.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:07.830
Sato-kagura, performed at local shrines,

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.790
takes many different forms throughout Japan.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:15.670
What's going on?

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:18.420
You never ask me to perform rituals.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:22.640
It's always me asking and you whining about it.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.350
What on Earth?

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:29.350
Oh.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:31.640
Whatever! Let's do it!

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.110
I love kagura!

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:38.110
You have to do it every now and then, anyway.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:41.110
It's best to do it when you're in the mood.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.200
It's a nice day today for a change, too.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.580
I bet the mountain gods will be happy.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:01.340
Hm? You're not wearing the special garb?

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.340
I'm doing it informally.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.390
Geez...

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:07.850
I'm starting it.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:08.640
Okay.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:14.600
Hi! How's everyone doing?

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.480
It's me, Jessica!

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.230
Let's do a special exercise today!

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:23.400
Dance to the beat and get the body you dream of!

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.870
Listen to the music!

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:28.620
Now it's getting exciting!

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.790
Feel it in your core!

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:34.000
Are you ready? One, two, here we go!

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.590
Shake! Your! Bo~dy! Shake it all up!

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.460
Oh! Oh! Shake! Shake! Give it a big shake!

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:42.510
Machi!

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.510
That's it! Keep it up!

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:43.970
This is a sacred ritual!

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:46.010
Don't mix diet dancing into it!

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:46.010
Now, one, two! One, two!

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:47.140
Let go of me!

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:50.430
I'm offering my flesh to the mountain gods!

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:50.430
Now, one, two! One, two!

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:53.180
Not fat! They don't want your fat!

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:56.190
Let go! What's wrong with fat?

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.190
Argh! I can't stand those bells.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.150
Just do it properly!

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:59.360
Let me go!

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:08.070
See that? The mountain gods are upset.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.120
Looks like it'll rain, but not yet.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:20.420
We can't let the boombox get wet.

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:25.880
The weather on the Sea of Japan side is worse than the Pacific's, right?

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:28.010
Hm? Yeah.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:32.390
It's cold, so we don't wanna move, so we stay at home, right?

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.730
We gain weight. We feel gloomy.

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:39.270
We suffer from foehn wind during the summer.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:41.690
It takes a while for the snow to melt.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:45.610
That's why I don't like the Sea of Japan side.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:48.360
What do you expect people to do about it?

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:51.410
Well, you're a miko.

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:54.870
Why don't you ask the mountain gods to make the climate nice?

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:56.580
Oh, stop it.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.080
I just do the stuff Grandma taught me.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:03.840
I'm an ordinary girl with no abilities or shamanistic powers at all.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.590
Oh? You don't remember?

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:08.970
When you were small...

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:16.480
Hm? Machi?

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:18.810
Are you getting up?

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.480
Want to go play somewhere?

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:24.730
Johnny Pamyu Pamyu.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:27.490
Ma—Whoa!

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.160
Yakata Nasutaka!

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:32.240
Pon-pon-pon! Pon-pon-pon-pon-pon-pon-pon!

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:35.490
You really scared me that time.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:37.620
Machi? Machi?!

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.370
What is that? What're you doing?!

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.460
Hey, Machi! Hey! Hey! Hey!

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.130
Eyelash extensions!

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.050
Eyelash extensions!

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.300
Eyelash extensions!

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:48.760
Ouch!

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:50.680
You're hurting me!

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:51.930
Eyelash extensions!

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:51.930
Ow!

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:55.510
And I've only recently realized...

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:57.430
the meaning of those words.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:02.480
And? What's the meaning of "Johnny Pamyu Pya..."

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.360
Pamyu... Pamyu Pya...

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:06.940
Gosh... That terrified me.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:06.940
Sunny Pamu Pyo...

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:13.700
On top of that, you had a couple other incidents when you were younger.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:09.400
Sunny Pamu...

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.910
Pyamu Pamu...

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.120
Pamu pyo...

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:17.700
That time with the landslide,
and with the buried gold.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.420
That's not true! You're just making those up.

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:25.750
You don't remember them
because you were in a trance.

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:28.460
I'd know if I fell into one, and I haven't!

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:35.390
Now the weather's getting worse. Let's go home.

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:38.180
Hey, Machi. Don't be like that.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:40.980
It's so hard to get you out here.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.900
No good. She's completely discouraged.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:57.080
Here's a fun fact: kagura originates from ancient Japan's divine possession rituals.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:01.000
Miko would spin into a trance, and this became kagura.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:06.090
By mastering kagura, anyone can enter a trance.

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:07.380
Especially you, Machi.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:08.750
No, I can't.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:13.630
Trance is really taking off in the Tokyo scene.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:18.890
You can't find a club without it.

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:21.560
Tokyo? Clubs?!

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.370
The dancing Kumamiko, number thirty-eight.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.990
Kamioroshi.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:46.040
Spin to the left!

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:46.830
Spin to the right!

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:51.670
Left, right, left, right!

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:52.670
Spin to the right!

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:53.970
Spin to the left!

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:55.970
Spin to the right! Spin to the right!

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:01.640
Even faster!

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:06.060
Right! Right! Right! Right!

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:08.310
Right! Right! Right right right right right right!

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:09.570
Jump!

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:20.410
I think I should have seen that coming.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:24.910
I... I'll perform a dance that suits me.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.920
Good, she's finally motivated.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:45.520
On Mount Kumade, you see bears.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:52.110
Girls are adorable.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:57.990
Old women are slow starters.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:14.510
Hi, Yoshio.

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:15.380
Hey!

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:18.590
Good work!

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:20.890
Why are you wearing that?

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:22.640
You look good in it.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:24.600
I don't appreciate that.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:27.770
I was helping the Women's Association bake cakes.

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:30.270
Look at this! I worked hard on it.

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:35.150
It's for you two.

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:35.610
Here.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:38.240
Forks are in the box.

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:38.650
Um...

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:41.120
I got you Afternoon Tea, too.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.540
See ya! Enjoy the cake.

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:45.540
Yoshio!

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:06.720
Is it good?

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:07.890
Yeah.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:09.850
I guess you'll be gaining weight.

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:12.900
It's your fault! You don't like whipped cream!

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:27.040
I'm so full. I can't eat another bite!

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:31.250
You'll turn into a cow if you sleep right after eating.

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:33.790
I'm not sleeping, just lying down.

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:56.020
The sky cleared up.

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:59.860
It's because you worked earnestly.

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:17.000
Two more sets! Here we go!

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:21.130
Rotate those hips to the left!

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:24.970
Spin those hips, yeah! To the right!

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:27.970
One, two, three, four!

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:31.680
How is it? Feel the burn in your abs?

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:37.650
One, two, three, four!

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:40.650
That's right! Keep it up!

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:45.070
Machi! Stop that!

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:00.840
It's been getting warm lately.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:05.760
Yeah. We're getting more sunny days too.

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:09.010
Actually, I'd say it's getting hot.

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:10.430
You think so?

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:12.180
I'm doing fine.

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:16.400
Natsu, I'll trim your fur.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:17.310
What?

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:20.020
You get worn out by the heat every year.

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:23.440
Shorter hair should help a little bit, right?

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.200
W-Well...

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:29.160
I think you should focus on school.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.330
High school entrance exams are coming up.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:32.580
You should study for them.

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:34.580
No need to worry about me.

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:39.630
Surprisingly, my grades are pretty good.

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:43.710
You're the only 8th grader at your school, so...

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:46.300
You know, Natsu...

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:51.720
It hurts to see you suffering from the heat every year.

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:54.810
If it affects you again this year,

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:57.520
I'll be too worried to study for entrance exams.

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:59.940
So, Natsu...

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:01.070
Machi...

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:06.700
This is rather elaborate.

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:09.450
We're in the precincts, so I used a screen.

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:12.700
I'm reminded of something else...

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:20.380
A charismatic hairdresser from Ginza!

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:23.920
Oh, no. I have a bad feeling about this.

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:25.920
Here we go!

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:30.970
Ow!

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:32.050
Ah.

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:34.560
Natsu!

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:36.890
Hey. Natsu!

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:36.890
Oh? What's going on?

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:38.520
Geez... Natsu!

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:40.400
'Sup, Machi!

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:41.860
Hi, Yoshio.

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:44.980
What are you doing with those scissors?

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.280
New miko garb?

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:49.400
That's right.

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:52.240
The old men of the village said they wanted to create

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:55.040
new miko garb that was cooler, since summer is coming.

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:59.540
We held a design competition in the village.

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:02.790
Maybe you could have told me.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:06.630
After careful judging, several finalists were chosen,

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:09.840
and the Women's Association sewed them with utmost care.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:14.180
And now you, the final judge, try them all on

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:16.720
and choose a winner for the summer.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:18.730
I'm the one deciding?

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:22.480
Of course. You're the one who'll be wearing it.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.440
Don't worry about it too much.

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:26.610
It's just old people killing time.

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:32.780
You <i>do</i> take off your short coat when it's hot,

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:35.080
which loses some of the Ainu heritage.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:37.120
Summer clothes will be nice.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:40.870
Exactly, Natsu! You make a good point.

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:44.250
So this pattern is associated with the Ainu?

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:47.300
I thought they were from Hokkaido.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.760
No, not just Hokkaido.

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:54.430
Tohoku has some villages named in the Ainu language.

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:59.430
In fact, I think our village has Ainu roots too.

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:02.730
But Grammy and the others won't let researchers in the village,

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:05.480
so I can't say for sure.

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:08.190
Oh...

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:10.610
That was almost exciting.

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:17.280
The Ainu, huh?

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:27.710
I can't wait to see the Ainu patterns they embroidered on these.

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:30.010
What? What? What?!

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:31.010
Hm?

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:34.590
What's wrong, Machi?

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:36.510
Natsu...

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:39.510
Is this outfit related to the Ainu?

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:41.560
I don't think so.

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.690
What? What's the matter?

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:51.820
Why?!

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:51.690
You creep!

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:54.400
Let go of me! You pervert!

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:54.400
Why is Natsu okay but not me?!

00:16:55.280 --> 00:17:00.660
Why?! Why am I a pervert but not Natsu? Give me a reason!

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:02.540
Stop it, Yoshio!

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:07.080
You're a human male.

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:10.840
Natsu is a bear.

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:16.220
Well, nothing I can do about that.

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:22.020
All that aside, what's this outfit?

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:23.560
This isn't Ainu!

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:25.100
It's not even miko garb.

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:27.850
That's because it's from a different category.

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:28.940
"A different category"?

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:29.020
Use white and red colors as a base.

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:29.020
No design restrictions.

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:30.440
The "Setting miko garb aside,

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:33.110
the idol outfit you want to see Machi wear" category!

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:35.900
The what? Why was that a category?

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:35.820
It should be a cute outfit that looks good on Machi.

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:39.990
You see, it struck me while
watching your kagura the other day.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:42.660
We should start an idol project for the—

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:43.500
Oh, shoot.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:45.410
What're you plotting? Don't even think about it!

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:47.170
Now, now, now, now...

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:51.550
We'll just make Matsu or someone wear it at the year-end party.

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:55.050
Let's check out the miko garb now, okay?

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:03.180
Now then, outfit number one.

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:06.980
Designed by Kumai Fumi, 86 years old.

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:10.190
Oh, she's pretty good!

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:13.190
She drew it splendidly despite her shaking hand!

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:16.030
You can feel her spirit in her scrawls!

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:17.740
I can't read this.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:20.070
Well then, Machi, please come out!

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.080
Whoa!

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.080
My, my...

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:32.710
The laurel crown is mystical!

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:35.710
The design evokes ancient times.

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:40.090
The sheer cloth makes you feel cool.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:43.100
Judges, what do you think?

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:46.180
Machi's cute!

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:50.560
Outfit two is designed by Kumai Mizuki, 7 years old.

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:53.520
Oh? She might be a budding manga author!

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:56.190
It's a very fancy design.

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:58.860
The highlight is the big ribbon.

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:01.870
It comes with bear ears and a bear tail!

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:05.660
What do you guys think?

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:08.660
Machi's cute!

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:11.080
Number three is...

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:16.050
Aww! Machi! You're so cute!

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:22.680
You look good in it! I made it for you!

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:24.050
Mom!

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:25.470
Here, hold this sunflower!

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:25.680
Mom!

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:28.980
You can't just do whatever you want!

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:31.190
What? But she looks so cute in it!

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:33.940
I wonder if I could make it a little shorter.

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:41.070
The last one is designed by Kumai Hifuo, 91 years old.

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:44.830
You can tell <i>his</i> hand was shaking quite a bit, too!

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:52.040
Her shoulders and back are boldly bared.

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:54.840
This design is a bit sexy.

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:56.710
Now she's tried them all.

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:59.210
Which was best, judges?

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:01.510
These are bear ears!

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:02.970
And this is a bear tail!

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:13.190
I like number two.

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:14.150
Huh?

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:18.400
I can't say I agree.

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:21.150
I do appreciate the ears and tail,

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:23.490
but it's not that good, really.

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:25.530
I'm all for number three.

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:28.700
Mom, your outfit is disqualified.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:29.450
What?

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:32.620
They're all embarrassing.

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:36.380
Why do you like number two so much, Yoshio?

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:38.630
She looks like an undiscovered idol.

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:41.420
That's too vague for me.

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:45.390
Be more specific, like, you like the ears, or the tail.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:49.100
Think carefully before picking number two.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:54.270
Everything else I've seen done before.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:52.980
The sunflower is good.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:56.100
Number three. Number three.

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:56.480
My dream is to break the mold

00:20:56.480 --> 00:21:02.280
and redefine the standard
image of the modern day miko.

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:05.530
With that in mind, I choose this!

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.620
That's a standard outfit somewhere else!

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:10.870
Yoshio, you just said you liked number two.

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:13.120
I wasn't <i>that</i> attached to it.

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:15.750
Number one's just as good for me.

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:17.630
You liked number one, so...

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:20.130
Well... hold on a sec.

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:23.970
We can't have a proper discussion if you just bend over.

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:25.970
Stand up for your own opinion.

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:28.800
Let's go over each design.

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:31.890
You liked number two, right, Yoshio?

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:34.060
Really, I'm fine with number one.

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:36.600
Why? You wanted number two at first.

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:38.520
I said, number one will do.

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:40.730
Don't do that.

00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:42.070
Why not?

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:46.280
We can't come to an agreement.

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:50.280
Machi, can you try number two ag—

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:51.280
No.

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:55.410
I'm not a dress-up doll.

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:29.670
Kumamiko-chan!

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:34.510
I'm a little hungry.

00:23:42.810 --> 00:23:44.110
Hmm...

00:23:44.110 --> 00:23:46.400
It seems I've lost my touch.

00:23:49.940 --> 00:23:54.990
Next Time: "Village Treasure"
